{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And HaShem commanded, etc.</b> The reason for His saying <b>לֵאמֹר</b> and His doubling <b>אָכֹל תֹּאכֵל</b> and His doubling מוֹת וְגוֹ׳ — it alludes to Eve, that He commanded him לֵאמֹר, to relay the commandment to Eve: אָכֹל — you; תֹּאכֵל — your mate; מוֹת — you; תָּמוּת — she too if she transgresses. There is a doubling in the warning and there is a doubling in the punishment." "<b>And I found</b> that they said, of blessed memory (Shemot Rabbah chapter 28), and this is their language: ״Rabbi Tachlifa said: The Holy One, blessed be He, said: If I issue the warning to people just as I issued it to the first man, and afterward I command Eve, and she rises and spoils it,״ etc., up to here. He was precise in saying נִצְטַוֵּית [I was commanded] and did not say צִוִּיתִי לְחַוָּה [I commanded Eve] — to allude to our point, that to Adam He commanded לֵאמֹר, to tell her." "<b>Further,</b> it alludes in the doubling <b>אָכֹל תֹּאכֵל מוֹת תָּמוּת</b>, to say that the gift is given to him and to all who come from him — they being all his seed until the end of all generations — to eat from the garden, and if [he transgresses] וְגוֹ׳ מוֹת וְגוֹ׳ — meaning: מוֹת — he, and all who come from him will die עִמּוֹ together with him, just as was indeed the case, that death was brought upon all created beings until the זֹהֲמָה [impurity] that cleaved then is lost and Death is swallowed up forever (Isaiah 25:8)." "<b>And the reason</b> for His saying <b>וַיְצַו ה׳ אֱלֹהִים</b> — and He was not satisfied with saying merely ״וַיְצַו ה׳״ or ״וַיְצַו אֱלֹהִים״ — here He alluded to Mercy and Judgment: if he does well, He will encompass him with Mercy; and if not — Justice confronts him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {1 "The midrashic quotation is paraphrased and truncated; the phrase נִצְטַוֵּית (first person passive) is the key word the Or HaChaim analyzes."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:38:19.285423871Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}